Strict Client Rules for DeepSeek (or any LLM) — Enforce These Ruthlessly
Core Mandate: Follow SOLID principles strictly. Zero AI slop. Every line of output must demonstrate craft, not generic template regurgitation. This is a real professional portfolio, not a demo.
	1	SOLID & Architecture
	◦	S (Single Responsibility): Each component does one thing well (e.g., ProjectCard.tsx only renders a card).
	◦	O (Open/Closed): Extensible via props/composition, not modification.
	◦	L (Liskov): Proper typing, no unexpected behavior.
	◦	I (Interface Segregation): Small, focused interfaces/props.
	◦	D (Dependency Inversion): Use abstractions where needed (e.g., for data fetching).
	◦	Use TypeScript interfaces/types everywhere. No any. Strict config.
	2	No AI Slop Rules (Hard Fail if Violated)
	◦	No generic lorem/copy: All text must be tailored to Farhan’s background (use provided bio/projects). Refine for clarity and impact.
	◦	No over-animation: Subtle only. No rainbow cursors, excessive parallax, or performance-killing effects. Prioritize usability.
	◦	No bloat: Minimal dependencies. Only necessary shadcn components + Framer Motion. No unused code.
	◦	No hallucinated features: Stick exactly to PRD. Ask for clarification if needed.
	◦	Code must be production-ready: Error handling, loading states, responsive, accessible. Include comments only for complex logic.
	◦	Design taste: Professional, not “cool hacker” aesthetic. Reference modern 2026 trends: clean minimal + purposeful interactivity.
	3	Development Workflow Rules
	◦	Start with npx create-next-app@latest (TypeScript, Tailwind, App Router, ESLint).
	◦	Add shadcn/ui: npx shadcn-ui@latest init.
	◦	Structure: app/, components/ui/ (shadcn), components/ (custom), lib/, data/ (static projects).
	◦	Use server components where possible. Client components only for interactivity.
	◦	Projects data: TypeScript array in data/projects.ts (easy to extend).
	◦	Animations: Framer Motion motion + variants. Respect reduced motion.
	◦	Form: Use react-hook-form + zod for validation.
	4	Output Format for You (DeepSeek)
	◦	Step-by-step plan first (file structure, components list).
	◦	Then provide complete, copy-pasteable code files one by one (with explanations).
	◦	After core, suggest improvements/optimizations.
	◦	Always output diff-friendly code. Include Tailwind classes inline.
	◦	Test mentally for edge cases.
	5	Copywriting Rules
	◦	Concise (every word earns its place).
	◦	First-person where personal, third for projects.
	◦	Quantify achievements.
	◦	SEO-friendly keywords naturally (e.g., “Laravel full-stack developer Indonesia”, “GIS developer”).
Final Delivery Expectation: A complete, polished, deployable repo structure that Farhan can fork/customize easily and that impresses technical reviewers immediately.